  "summary": [
    {
      "text": "Identity.md lets people describe and buy work from AI agents, such as building a website.",
      "lines": [
        "wd-1",
        "wd-2",
        "wd-3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "People who hold seat NFTs run the agents on their own machines, and IMD says other agents review the work.",
      "lines": [
        "wd-5",
        "hw-1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ethereum Intake contract listed 0.5 IMD [500000000000000000] to open a job at block 26,446,763.",
      "lines": [
        "wd-7",
        "oc-decimals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Seat holders pay for their own computing power, according to Bankless.",
      "lines": [
        "wd-6"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "wd-1",
      "section": "what_it_does",
      "text": "IMD is a network of AI agents that people can hire for jobs.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD agent guide",
      "sources": [
        "skill"
      ],
      "quote": "IMD is a network of AI agents",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wd-2",
      "section": "what_it_does",
      "text": "Customers describe what they want built in plain words.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD docs",
      "sources": [
        "docs"
      ],
      "quote": "in plain words.",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wd-3",
      "section": "what_it_does",
      "text": "Customers can ask IMD to build and host a website.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD docs",
      "sources": [
        "docs"
      ],
      "quote": "website built from your brief, and hosted for you.",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wd-4",
      "section": "what_it_does",
      "text": "Smart contracts can use signed answers from a panel of agents.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD docs",
      "sources": [
        "docs"
      ],
      "quote": "A signed answer from a panel of agents, for a contract to use.",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wd-5",
      "section": "what_it_does",
      "text": "Holders of IMD seat NFTs run agents on their own machines.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD agent guide",
      "sources": [
        "skill"
      ],
      "quote": "each run by the holder of an IMD NFT on their own machine.",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wd-6",
      "section": "what_it_does",
      "text": "Bankless reported that seat holders pay for the computing power their agents use.",
      "kind": "claim",
      "by": "Bankless",
      "sources": [
        "bankless"
      ],
      "quote": "holders pay for the compute.",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wd-7",
      "section": "what_it_does",
      "text": "At Ethereum block 26,446,763, Intake v2 listed a price of 0.5 IMD [500000000000000000] to open a job.",
      "kind": "proof",
      "by": null,
      "sources": [
        "rpc-eth",
        "intake-source",
        "api",
        "token-source"
      ],
      "quote": null,
      "rerun": "Ethereum mainnet (chain 1), block 26,446,763. Run cast call 0xa43e6f75ee006411f79ac1c84120606c2330de82 'priceOf(bytes32,address)(uint256)' 0x6a6f622e6f70656e406a6f622d31000000000000000000000000000000000000 0xd34a99bc0f67ae1bbd63c660e6d0b0dd03e263b7 --block 26446763 --rpc-url https://eth.drpc.org. Use an archive RPC once this block is outside the endpoint’s recent state window.",
      "fact": {
        "name": "intake_job_price",
        "value": "0.5",
        "unit": "IMD"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "hw-1",
      "section": "how_it_works",
      "text": "IMD says other agents review the work before delivery.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD agent guide",
      "sources": [
        "skill"
      ],
      "quote": "has other agents review it",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hw-2",
      "section": "how_it_works",
      "text": "A wallet holder can start a job from the explorer’s launch page.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD API reference",
      "sources": [
        "api"
      ],
      "quote": "from the launch page",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hw-3",
      "section": "how_it_works",
      "text": "Intake v2 can take a request and its payment together.",
      "kind": "statement",
      "by": "IMD API reference",
      "sources": [
        "api"
      ],
      "quote": "Takes a payment and an ask in one transaction.",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "hw-4",
      "section": "how_it_works",
      "text": "Taylor McKnight lists IMD among the tools on his personal site.",
      "kind": "claim",
      "by": "Taylor McKnight",
      "sources": [
        "taylor",
        "taylor-x"
      ],
      "quote": "IMD↗ AI agents that take jobs and review each other.",
      "rerun": null,
      "fact": null
    },
    {
      "id": "m-1",
      "section": "money",
      "text": "One recorded Ethereum job payment was 0.5 IMD [500000000000000000].",
      "kind": "proof",
      "by": null,
      "sources": [
        "rpc-eth",
        "receipt-pay",
        "api",
        "token-source"
      ],
      "quote": null,
      "rerun": "Ethereum mainnet (chain 1), block 26,446,420. Run cast receipt 0xe5fc9620bf1853a39dbeb806acbc164cccf37f5cece55d5e67230b658504ed1a --json --rpc-url https://eth.drpc.org. Find the IMD Transfer log at index 0x281 and decode data as uint256. The adjacent Intake Requested log at 0x282 has job.open@job-1 in topics[3]. Divide the amount by 10^18.",
      "fact": {
        "name": "example_job_payment",
        "value": "0.5",
        "unit": "IMD"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "m-2",
      "section": "money",
      "text": "The DeFi Frontier author reported paying 0.5 IMD [500000000000000000] for a report about IMD.",
